    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d918">

                <pb facs="1732" n="1692" xml:id="pg1692"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">674.84A/11–1054: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 918<lb/>The Ambassador in Egypt (Caffery) to the Department of State
                        <anchor n="1" xml:id="d918-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Cairo</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1954-11-10T15:00:00+02:00">November 10, 1954—3 p.m.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush">Confidential</p>
                <p>637. As I reported in mytel 617,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d918-f2"/> I spoke to
                    Minister Foreign Affairs last Saturday about Tel Aviv’s 398.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d918-f3"/> I spoke again to him this morning along lines Deptel
                        705.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d918-f4"/> Fawzi said that in meantime he had
                    spoken to Prime Minister, Minister Interior, etc. They all agree that every
                    effort should be made to prevent incidents in Gaza area. On one hand they do not
                    deny that there are infiltrations from Gaza side. On other hand they forcefully
                    insist that Israelis are exaggerating their number and importance.</p>
                <p>They insist also that for some time they have been taking appropriate measures to
                    control infiltrations. They will redouble their efforts in that direction. They
                    definitely do not want trouble with Israel.</p>
                <p>In this connection GOE has always indicated willingness enter into cooperative
                    control arrangements between local police commanders. However, when General
                    Burns recently attempted to call meeting for this purpose, Israelis indicated
                    they were not ready to hold such discussions now (see Embdesps 858, November 5
                    and 886, November 10).<anchor n="5" xml:id="d918-f5"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed> Caffery </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
